+# Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling It Is Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined "changing or cancelling a visit once booked", and the 2026-08-08 decision confirmed the whole row as deliberate. That row bundles two capabilities under one line: amendment and cancellation. The sample can therefore create a visit but never correct one, so a mistyped date or a wrong description stands permanently.
+
+The owner reopened the row on 2026-08-15 and split it. The 2026-08-08 ADR reserved exactly this path: narrowing a row is an owner decision recorded in its own non-goal ADR.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-5 whole.** Rejected: the owner has decided otherwise, and the row's two halves carry different costs.
+2. **Open the whole row.** Build amendment and cancellation together. Rejected: cancellation is the half that adds lifecycle state, which the sample carries nowhere.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, recorded as REQ-VISITEDIT-001. Cancelling a booked visit remains out of scope under NG-5, and NG-4 is untouched: nothing is deleted.
+
+A correction is held to the booking rules and updates the visit in place. The visit keeps its identity, so the pet gains no second record.
+
+The form is reachable by its address alone. The owner declined a visible entry point in this request and named a follow-up request as the place for one.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The sample now demonstrates correction on all three records it holds: owner, pet, and visit.
+- NG-5 covers one capability instead of two, and its wording no longer bundles them.
+- No lifecycle state enters the domain. A visit is either booked or corrected; there is no cancelled state.
+- The correction form is unreachable by navigation until a follow-up request adds a link. Four questions the request left open are recorded in the PRD.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [REQ-VISITEDIT-001: Correcting a booked visit](../prd.md#req-visitedit-001) — the requirement this decision opens.
+
+## References
+
+- [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) — the decision this one narrows.
