@@ -104,15 +106,29 @@ Each pet is recorded against exactly one owner, with a name, a birth date, and a
 
 A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
 
+<a id="req-visitedit-001"></a>
+
+A booked visit can be corrected. Its date and its description are opened again on the same form used for booking, prefilled with what the visit currently holds, and a mistyped date or a wrong reason is fixed rather than left standing `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. A correction is held to the same rules as booking, and it changes the visit already on the pet's record instead of adding a second one. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope (NG-5). In this requirement the correction form is reached only by going to its address directly: no page of the system links to it, and the owner's record page is unchanged.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when its correction form is opened, then the form shows that visit's current date and description.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a booked visit, when a description and a date later than today are submitted, then that visit carries the new values and the reader is returned to the owner's record.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given an accepted correction, when the owner's record is shown, then the pet holds the same number of visits as before the correction.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the description is named, and the form is shown again.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then it is refused, the date is named, and the form is shown again.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a refused correction, when the form is shown again, then the stored visit still holds its previous date and description.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Correcting a visit that does not exist, or one that belongs to another pet, is refused rather than opening or changing an unrelated record.
+4. A visit whose date has already passed is still held to the future-date rule: a correction that keeps the passed date is refused.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Is In Scope; Cancelling It Is Not](adr/2026-08-15-non-goal-visit-correction.md)
 
